     "transversal",
     "corresponding",
     "alternate"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A line that crosses two lines is a transversal. When it crosses two parallel lines it makes pairs of equal angles.\nCorresponding angles are equal, alternate interior angles are equal and co-interior angles add up to 180 degrees.\nVertically opposite angles are always equal."
    }
